Here I was happy to have gotten my hands on the source to 2.3e and now after
spending a summer holiday adding features I find the great 3.0 release is out.
Ok I can get it soon.

Right now I notice that the gods may revive a dead player.
That was one of the options I added. I tend to play very quickly and often
fall prey to stupid traps 
1) dead cockatrice/trap door
2) hell and back / fight gremlins / burn in hell
3) I even over eat on occasion
I added code that would (possibly) revive the player and polymorph him into
something strange. For 1) piercer 2) demon or wraith 3) orc.
There was also the possibility of the gods reviving you for a normal death.
These routines used polyself() so you eventually returned to human.
The most fun for this was the messages ...
The gods, greatly amused, revive you for some more fun. (etc)
and some messages describing near death experiences.

That was a fun patch.
My more serious patch (to zap.c) was to black dragons -- disintegrate rays.
These kill on the first hit, like finger of death or wand of death. I gave
the dragon a weaker version - if you were wearing armor (cloak/suit, gloves
don't count) the disintegrate breath destroys all your armor. This gives
you a change to go 'Holy -explitive-' and ^T right out of there.
Before the patch we often ended up with bones files with 4+ dead players and
a Black dragon. No fun, but great to loot.

Does anything like exist for version 3.0?

